<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-3-6" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>External Forces and Resonance</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      We now apply the method of undetermined coefficients to a physical setting:
      a mass-spring system driven by a sinusoidal external force. The behavior of
      the solution depends critically on whether the forcing frequency matches the
      system's natural frequency, a a phenomenon called <term>resonance</term>.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="./3-6/sec1-external-force-setup.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="./3-6/sec2-external-force-examples.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="./3-6/sec3-resonance.ptx"/>

</section>
